<p>Israeli naval forces intercepted part of the Gaza-bound Global Sumud Flotilla in international waters near Greece and detained activists, Israeli authorities and organizers said Thursday. Israel’s Foreign Ministry said about 175 people were detained, while flotilla organizers said 211 people were “kidnapped”. The flotilla sought to breach Israel’s naval blockade of Gaza, which Israel says is lawful and necessary to stop weapons reaching the enclave. Organizers said the boarding was illegal because it happened far from Gaza in international waters. The incident drew protests and condemnation from several governments and advocacy groups. The United States criticized the flotilla as a counterproductive initiative.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/kj_uZcTgW070gSWkC92swHRRQ93C20o3vglNpHiJlkeLnkSlfgG2yE3ogI7TuuXH_lFuPEbpZeovU4RfC8Uj2fCHSF7fckSWD17wbJjQFLso7FSfvrEs0TLpsDAlgg9R8vWXdrbeo2LLR3yw1hqyxRfWoQaebE1X_8XSuVhvIaDDmAnUGyRFJoTCiuwcSilLvKk9uANWWN18EL8vAdQPo9Ud5uNhJ8Vm3D5ZAFSou2sLa7WN_EwhCJlcGSqaRXC4UqiQkqZSs2MahSPmqA' alt='This grab from black and white CCTV footage shows members on flotilla boat with hands in air as Israeli forces intercepted activists who set sail earlier this month from Barcelona attempting to break Israel’s maritime blockade of Gaza, near the southern Greek island of Crete, early Thursday, April 30, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Boarding claims: The flotilla said forces used speedboats, lasers, communications jamming and orders for participants to kneel, while Israel said the operation caused no casualties.</li><li>Distance disputed: Organizers said the interception happened hundreds of miles from Gaza, with several reports placing the operation roughly 965 km to more than 1,000 km from the enclave.</li><li>Foreign detainees: The passenger list included a Paris city councillor, 11 French nationals, seven Irish citizens, two Canadians and citizens from several other countries.</li><li>Safety accounts: Israel said those taken from the vessels were unharmed; organizers alleged some damaged vessels were left at sea as a storm approached.</li></ul><blockquote>Israel will not allow the breach of the lawful naval blockade on Gaza. - Gideon Saar</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israel’s Foreign Ministry: The ministry dismissed the flotilla as a publicity stunt and said early intervention was needed to keep the vessels from getting closer to Gaza. (<a href='https://humenglish.com/latest/israel-intercepts-gaza-bound-flotilla-near-crete-detains-over-170-activists/'>Hum English</a>)</li><li>Global Sumud Flotilla activist Omer Aslan: Aslan said Israel’s interception would not deter the flotilla movement from trying to reach Gaza. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/30/flotilla-activist-israels-brutal-attack-will-not-deter-us'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Greek Foreign Ministry: Greece said it asked Israel to withdraw its vessels from the area and offered to receive passengers on Greek territory and ensure their safe return. (<a href='https://www.brecorder.com/news/40419137/israel-intercepts-gaza-aid-ships-in-international-waters'>Business Recorder</a>)</li><li>Reporters Without Borders: RSF condemned the detention of journalists aboard the flotilla and said Israel’s army was responsible for their safety. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/30/rsf-condemns-kidnapping-of-three-journalists-on-board-gaza-aid-flotilla'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/canada/article-canadians-detained-by-israel-gaza-flotilla/'>Two Canadians among activists detained after Israel intercepts Gaza aid flotilla</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639327-israel-rsf-journalists-gaza/'>Reporters Without Borders slams Israel for ‘abducting’ journalists</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/5/1/condemnation-and-protests-against-israels-raid-of-gaza-aid-flotilla'>Condemna